Hello Robert,

I hope this email finds you doing well and having a good week. Thank you fo=
r taking the time to review my email. Robert Half is looking to hire for on=
e of our top clients in your market for a Sr. Golang Developer-AI Agent pos=
ition.

For consideration, please email an updated resume to brandon.goldberg@rober=
thalf.com<mailto:brandon.goldberg@roberthalf.com> or reply to this email wi=
th an updated resume. If you are not interested in this opportunity, please=
 feel free to forward this to anyone you think would be a great fit.
Pay: $60-$70/hr W2 (Flexible); Must be USC or Green Card only; no sponsorsh=
ip or C2C provided with this position
Duration: 8/24/26-10/31/26; Approximately 30 hours/week (can fluctuate betw=
een 20-40 hours/week)
Location: Fully remote
This role is ideal for a senior-level Golang engineer with hands-on experie=
nce building AI agents and LLM-powered applications in production environme=
nts. The team is building an AI-driven solution that supports quarterly acc=
ess reviews, evidence validation workflows, and enterprise integrations, wo=
rking closely with existing engineering teams.

Must-Have Skills

*        Strong hands-on Golang/Go development experience

*        Experience building production AI agents or agentic applications

*        LLM integration experience (Claude, Anthropic, OpenAI, or similar)

*        Backend development expertise including APIs and distributed syste=
ms

*        Experience designing agent workflows, orchestration, tool/function=
 calling, and context management

*        Cloud-native development experience (Kubernetes, Docker, AWS, etc.=
)

*        Strong communication skills and ability to work independently with=
 engineering teams


Responsibilities

*        Write production code in Go

*        Build backend services, APIs, and distributed systems

*        Design and integrate AI agents into enterprise applications

*        Build integration between agents, services, APIs, and data sources

*        Work with Claude Gateway and enterprise LLM environments

*        Support access review and evidence validation workflows

*        Integrate Slack notifications and communications capabilities

*        Collaborate closely with Salesforce engineers and Protiviti techni=
cal teams

*        Participate in architecture discussions, development, testing, and=
 delivery activities


Qualifications:

*        Strong production Go development experience

*        Demonstrated experience personally building AI agents, not just co=
nsuming LLM APIs

*        Backend architecture and API development expertise

*        Understanding of agent orchestration, tool calling, and workflow d=
esign

*        Experience operating in cloud-native environments

*        Strong software engineering fundamentals

Preferred Qualifications:

*        Claude / Anthropic experience

*        Agentic frameworks and advanced agent architectures

*        Slack API integrations

*        Enterprise workflow automation experience

*        IAM, security, access management, or identity systems experience

*        Kubernetes and containerized application deployment


If you or someone you know are interested in being considered this open pos=
ition, please reply to this email with a current copy of your resume. I wil=
l carefully review ALL resumes and ONLY follow up with those candidates who=
 are a best match for this role.


Sincerely,
Brandon Goldberg
Senior Technical Recruiter
National Technology Accounts
